MIT License

This repository contains work derived from the Omarchy project
(https://github.com/basecamp/omarchy), which is MIT licensed, alongside
original work. Because the mix differs per file, the derivation is named
per path rather than claimed in one blanket sentence. Line counts are
against Omarchy 4.0.0.r1744 unless noted.

`packages/forks` is this repo's own record of the upstream files the rice
copies or couples to, with the SHA-256 each carried when the dependency was
last verified. It is the authority on what is derived and is kept current by
`loaf forks --record`; this notice names the paths but does not restate it.

Upstream Omarchy's work, carried verbatim
-----------------------------------------

  .config/hypr/xdph.conf
      Byte-identical to config/hypr/xdph.conf (4 lines). Tracked so `loaf
      heal` catches its displacement, not to change anything in it.

  .config/hypr/hyprsunset.conf
      Upstream's config/hypr/hyprsunset.conf (14 lines), carried as it stood
      before the quattro migration. The only lines that differ from the
      installed copy are a stale comment about autostarting hyprsunset; no
      setting differs.

Upstream Omarchy's work, with modifications by Austin Karren
------------------------------------------------------------

Each file below began as upstream's and was modified in place: the comment
scaffold and the shape are upstream's, the values and additions are this
rice's.

  .config/hypr/input.conf
      From upstream's stock user input config (54 lines). Upstream's are the
      structure, the commented-out examples and the prose. Modified: the
      settings actually enabled (compose:caps, repeat rate and delay,
      clickfinger, touchpad scroll factor) and three added lines — the
      per-terminal scroll_touchpad window rules.

  .config/hypr/hyprland.lua
      From config/hypr/hyprland.lua (43 lines). Upstream's are the bootstrap
      `dofile`, the `require("default.hypr.omarchy")` load and the
      override-require shape that makes personal files load after the
      defaults. Modified: the require list names this repo's own modules,
      including windows.lua, which stock quattro has no counterpart for, and
      a trailing block pins the single-window aspect ratio to 6:5 while
      leaving upstream's toggle mechanism entirely alone (shokupan-plugins
      ADR-0026).

  .config/chromium-flags.conf
      The four flag lines are upstream's, adopted verbatim when the file was
      brought into the repo (20 lines total, the rest being the comment that
      explains why it is tracked — ADR-0036).

Original work by Austin Karren
------------------------------

Written for this repository, overriding Omarchy through the extension points
it documents rather than copying its implementations:

  .local/bin/                    (the `loaf` CLI)
  .config/hypr/bindings.lua      .config/hypr/looknfeel.lua
  .config/hypr/windows.lua       .config/hypr/monitors.lua
  .config/hypr/autostart.lua     .config/omarchy/hooks/
  .config/uwsm/env.d/            .config/bash/
  .local/share/applications/     .config/omarchy/extensions/
  migrations/                    packages/
  docs/                          test/
  README.md                      .XCompose

Two of these borrow a shape without copying content, and are recorded in
`packages/forks` as watches rather than forks:
`.config/bash/50-omarchy-rc.sh` and `.config/bash/env.d/00-omarchy.sh` each
carry the guard shape from upstream's own `default/bashrc` and
`/etc/skel/.bashrc` so the two stay comparable (ADR-0042). Every glyph
codepoint in `.config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc` was extracted
from upstream's menu or the pre-quattro palette rather than retyped, and its
overrides restate the upstream fields they keep because upstream's
mergeMenuSources() copies keys rather than merging them.

